    "show_share": true,
    "description": "For Maureen Ouko, the path to a career in nursing wasn't paved with textbooks or classroom lectures. It was forged in the hospital corridors where she spent countless hours by her mother's side during her battle with chronic myeloid leukemia. As a child, she initially held a negative view of nurses, but that perspective shifted dramatically as she witnessed the quiet dedication and empathy of the health care professionals who cared for her mother.",
